#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
QAI-DCDMAC: Cyberism-enabled Quantum-AI Adaptive Directional MAC for IoT networks
=================================================================================
Frame-based Python simulator that implements the methodology of the paper:

  * hierarchical tree network (sink -> parents -> children), M-beam directional antennas
  * state construction S_t (Eq. 1, 5), normalisation (Eq. 6)
  * quantum-enhanced feature map: amplitude encoding (Eq. 7), parameterised circuit U(theta)
    (Eq. 8), expectation values of observables (Eq. 9), concatenation S'_t (Eq. 10).
    The circuit is simulated exactly with a 3-qubit real state-vector simulator (NumPy only)
  * Deep Q-Network agent (pure NumPy, replay buffer, target net, Adam) (Eq. 11-12)
  * reward function (Eq. 13-18)
  * adaptive slot scheduling score Omega_i (Eq. 19-20)
  * directional transmission with argmax beam selection (Eq. 21-22)
  * per-node duty-cycle adaptation (Eq. 23-25)
  * Cyberism closed loop: Observe -> Learn -> Schedule -> Transmit -> Update (Eq. 2, Alg. 1)
  * baselines: S-MAC, DCD-MAC, RL-MAC (tabular Q-learning duty cycle), and an ablation
    "DQN-DCD" (same as QAI-DCDMAC but without the quantum features)
  * metrics (Eq. 37-42): throughput, delay, PDR, reliability, energy, lifetime, overhead
  * experiments: node-density sweep (Fig. 5) and traffic-load sweep (Fig. 6)

Usage
-----
    pip install numpy matplotlib
    python qai_dcdmac_sim.py demo                  # one quick run of every protocol
    python qai_dcdmac_sim.py density --seeds 3     # Fig. 5 style experiment
    python qai_dcdmac_sim.py load --seeds 3        # Fig. 6 style experiment
    python qai_dcdmac_sim.py all --seeds 3 --jobs 4
    python qai_dcdmac_sim.py all --quick           # small/fast sanity run
    add --ablation to include the DQN-without-quantum baseline

NOTE: all numbers come from this simulator's own radio / energy model. They show the
trends of the proposed design but will not reproduce the paper's exact figures.
"""
